    "body": "Part of #458; preserves the separate owner acceptance on #276 and #325.\n\nThe launcher could abort a valid ownership check at 15 seconds despite a configured 60-second startup allowance, and it could deadlock by waiting for helper exit before draining redirected output. A native baseline reproduction fails on four valid slow ownership probes; the candidate completes the precheck and starts the matching disposable gateway.\n\nDrain both streams in bounded chunks, retain at most 256 KiB of UTF-8 protocol stdout, and require exit zero plus complete valid output. Initial helper allowance is `max(15, StartupTimeoutSeconds)`; ownership retries share the remaining monotonic release budget. Initial failures identify the helper stage, timing, output sizes and exit status without logging raw output. An inconclusive recheck retains the last verified held owner and complete safety guidance. Slow successful checks leave metadata. API, ownership decisions, stored formats and configuration remain unchanged.\n\nValidation at `b6ed79eeb289b781c48d3b0f994c1b2577990df9`: 27/27 native checks; independent focused QA and mutation checks; tooling lint and repository formatting passed. The preceding implementation also passed actual built-API slow ownership/startup/both-shells/managed-drain QA and all CI jobs. [Exact-head CI](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/actions/runs/43546076967) is fully green: Gates (including all coverage thresholds, licenses, generated docs and dependency audit), Browser, Windows launcher and Template image. Unchanged local Windows symlink/POSIX/SQLite test limitations are recorded in the [evidence directory](docs/qa/2026-11-13-launcher-timeouts/README.md); the complete Linux gate passed.\n\nClaude Opus 5.5 xhigh completed diagnosis/design review, one full implementation review and one [targeted correction review](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/460#issuecomment-6870208840). Both full-review findings are fixed and mutation-verified; the targeted verdict is READY with no introduced blocker. Existing helper-descendant cleanup remains follow-up #459. The exact historical stalled helper is unrecorded; reproduced defects are not claimed as proof of the original incident.\n\nLocal repair and owner cold-launch QA: the reviewed executable is installed; configuration and all three shortcut hashes are preserved. At the owner's request, two separate normal drains confirmed process exit, closed port and released locks before the owner launched first the desktop shortcut, then the taskbar icon. Both cold launches succeeded, produced new gateway PIDs and returned 200 for health and both app shells. The final gateway is left running. Automated installed-launch execution was policy-blocked; no workaround was attempted, and the owner performed both actual clicks. No migration or reset occurred. Implementation, reviews, independent QA, CI and local cold-launch acceptance are complete. Merge awaits explicit owner authorization.",
